/-! # The numerical inequality (6.4): `λ M₀ - I(ρ) + C* ≤ U`

Only *lower* bounds for logarithms are needed. They come from the series
`log ((1+x)/(1-x)) = 2 ∑ x^(2k+1)/(2k+1)`, whose terms are nonnegative for `0 ≤ x < 1`, so that
partial sums are lower bounds, together with Mathlib's `Real.log_two_lt_d9` for the range
reduction `log y = log (2^k y) - k log 2`. The certificates (`k`, partial sums with 10 terms,
rounded down) were generated by exact rational arithmetic; `norm_num` checks each one.
-/

public section

